{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/237130-the-serendipitous-created-the-extempore","id":237130,"title":"The Serendipitous Created: The Extempore","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-22T10:41:37-07:00","id":237130,"title":"The Serendipitous Created: The Extempore","content":"Hallo. Recently, I was invited to partake in a Promethean game, and after being told that another player was going to be an Osiran (my original idea), I got to thinking about creating an Extempore instead.<br /> My current idea is something along the lines of a Promethean-Construct, created from the wood of a thousands of years old tree, which had been worshipped throughout its life and lost in a catalysmic forest fire, possibly caused by a Firestorm. This is in a nutshell of course.<br /> <br /> If it isn't immidiately obvious, I'd like to discuss the Extempore. Does this seem like a proper Extempore? Have you used them? If so, how? Have you let players use them/used them yourself as a player? How do you recon an Extempore PC would influence/change a Throng of otherwise traditional Prometheans? Do you have any cool ideas for Extempores yourself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T00:45:06-07:00","id":238003,"title":"","content":"Sure, that sounds like a reasonable origin of an extempore, although I think the pyros would be more likely to make the promethean out of wood and a corpse or two, since pyros seems to prefer the human form for this sort of thing, but that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T06:46:45-07:00","id":238151,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I had thought that he would be a strange amalgam between the lost priest, who had refused to abandon the tree, despite the fire, and who had died desperately trying to fend the flames away. Sadly, my GM didn't fancy an Extempore to start out with.<br /> I can sorta understand him.<br /> <br /> Do you have any experience with useing the Extempore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T21:18:40-07:00","id":238832,"title":"","content":"Sadly not, I'd need help coming up with it anyway, I'm fine with thinking up abilities, but coming up with something balanced against the other bestowments? Not part of m skill set sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T16:47:26-07:00","id":240893,"title":"","content":"I agree that this could make a very good Extempore. Because as written the Extempore have a &quot;Disquiet-like&quot; affect on other Prometheans, I can kind of see why your ST turned it down (assuming he didn't want to just handwave that particular bit).<br /> <br /> Have you thought of what sort of Bestowment this character would have? As an Extempore, they would have a very unique one. Something that came to mind to me was the ability to interact with plant spirits. You could call that Bestowment Veriditas, after the alchemical term. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viridity\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viridity</a><br /> <br /> I think the concept could also work as an Ulgan Construct. I believe there is even a similar example in the book where constructs are discussed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}